# Riverglades for the Horde, part 1 of 4 (2026-11-12; the Horde route since 0.4.0). Hand-written from players'
# recordings of the zone (123 sessions to 2026-11-12) and Forever's quest data (the client's quest records,
# QuestieDB 1.0.16 and EG Link) for titles, levels, objectives and places.
# Order: the way in on foot from Kargath through Twilight's Shroud (after the Stranglethorn Vale & Swamp of Sorrows
# guide, about level 42: a flight from Stonard to Kargath, then Rog'mar first and Sleebo's workshop), or by the goblin
# boat from Tanaris for a character without Kargath's flight path (Powderfuse Port, Sleebo's workshop, then Rog'mar);
# Rog'mar (flight path, inn), Neza Bloodsnout's three hunts on the plains with Sleebo's marsh on the first one, a western loop
# (Turner's Logging Camp, the Bristle Hills, Gelinda Coppergleam's Cinderscale hollow, Meadowsbrook) and the hearth
# home, the training grounds, then the river and the Farholde training camp.
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (players' recordings): Poison Tips after Feathers for Fletching,
# A Hunter's Quiver after Poison Tips, Gnoll Infestation, Bristle Hills Bandits and Snargl's Snout after A Hunter's
# Quiver; A Gift From Our Enemies after Food for the Taking; Show Them How It's Done after both of Krom'rosh's first
# quests; A Serving of Strength after A Gift From Our Enemies; Stick 'Em after Fetch 'n' Fletch; The Goblin Trader
# after Borrowed Blades; Rock 'em and Sock 'em after Gaseous Gold; Tran'gul's quests after Show Them How It's Done
# (part 2).
# Elites, each behind a group choice: Snargl (40), Ombassa (41), Ghostmaw (42); Scoutmaster Vargas (42) in part 2.
# Picked up on the way here: Report to Rog'mar (95141, Commander Aggro'gosh at Grom'gol, in the Stranglethorn Vale
# guide). Taken here for the next guide: On the Other Side (95033, Tan'jani, for Camp Mojache) and Shipping and
# Handling (95296, Friz, for Steamwheedle Port), both on the Feralas & Tanaris guide's way.
# Twice Misplaced Trust (97332): Wharfmaster Lozgil in Booty Bay offers it after Anything of Value (97328) and
#   Zimmix's Great Escape (97331), both done in the 30-40 Stranglethorn guide; the Stranglethorn Vale guide's first
#   Booty Bay stop takes it and Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz takes it on the first port stop here.
# Left out on purpose:
# - Hail the Dragonslayer (95936): it starts from the head of Scaldaron, a rare elite drake in the Cinderscale
#   hollow.
# - Finding Tan'jani (95143), from Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands: this guide doesn't assume you carry it;
#   While-you're-here hands it in when you have it.

step Fly to Kargath
  when taxi "Kargath"
  when zone "Swamp of Sorrows"
  zone Swamp of Sorrows
  tip The Riverglades lie south of the Badlands. Ride east from the Harborage to Stonard and fly to Kargath: the way down into the zone starts there.
  goto 46.1,54.7 "Stonard flight master"
  fly "Kargath"
  zone Badlands

step Into the Riverglades
  when taxi "Kargath"
  when !zone "Riverglades"
  zone Badlands
  tip New in Forever: this guide follows what players did in the Riverglades. If a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip From Kargath, ride south-east across the Badlands to the zone's southern edge: the pass of Twilight's Shroud leads down into the Riverglades. Rog'mar, the Horde's fort, stands in the middle of the zone, east along the valley.
  goto 55.0,93.0 "Into the Riverglades"
  zone Riverglades
  enter "Riverglades" @32.0,29.9

step Fly to Freewind Post
  when !taxi "Kargath"
  when !zone "Riverglades"
  tip New in Forever: this guide follows what players did in the Riverglades. If a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip The Riverglades lie across the sea from Tanaris: a goblin boat sails from Steamwheedle Port, north-east of Gadgetzan, to Powderfuse Port. Fly to Freewind Post in Thousand Needles and head south-east through the Shimmering Flats to Gadgetzan. (If you already know Kargath in the Badlands, the way in through Twilight's Shroud works too.)
  fly "Freewind Post"

step Gadgetzan
  when !taxi "Kargath"
  when !zone "Riverglades"
  zone Tanaris
  tip Learn Gadgetzan's flight path: it saves the ride next time.
  getfp "Gadgetzan"

step Boat to Powderfuse Port
  when !taxi "Kargath"
  when !zone "Riverglades"
  zone Tanaris
  tip Steamwheedle Port is on the coast north-east of Gadgetzan: wait on the pier for the goblin boat to Powderfuse Port.
  goto 67.57,23.1 "Boat to Powderfuse Port"

step Powderfuse Port
  when !taxi "Kargath"
  zone Riverglades
  tip New in Forever: if a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip Friz Frazzlespark keeps a stall at the west end of the docks. The port's other jobs are for later in this guide: this crate goes to the Horde's fort.
  accept 95062                          -- Frazzlespark's Crate: for Krom'rosh in Rog'mar

step Rog'mar
  tip West to Rog'mar, the Horde's fort in the middle of the zone. Neza Bloodsnout stands on its east side, Kreza Darkthorn and Krom'rosh in the middle with Grakna, the wind rider master; Innkeeper Toka and Tan'jani on the west side.
  accept 96107                          -- Neza Bloodsnout: Feathers for Fletching
  accept 93788                          -- Kreza Darkthorn: Borrowed Blades
  turnin 95141                          -- Krom'rosh: Aggro'gosh's report from Grom'gol, if you carry it
  accept 93786                          -- A Message in Blood
  accept 93787                          -- Food for the Taking
  getfp "Rog'mar" npc 255993            -- Grakna, in the middle of the fort
  sethome "Rog'mar" npc 256675         -- Innkeeper Toka
  accept 95951                          -- Tan'jani: Fetch 'n' Fletch

step Krom'rosh
  when onquest 95062
  tip Frazzlespark's crate from the port goes to Krom'rosh, in the middle of the fort.
  turnin 95062                          -- Krom'rosh

step The plains and the marsh
  tip South-east of Rog'mar the plains run down to Terral's Watch. The Low Plains Buzzards circle everywhere; a picked carcass lies in the grass (its skull starts A Feast for Buzzards), and the marsh vents are just past it.
  collect 271793 x6 quest 96107.1       -- Plains Buzzard Feather

step Neza Bloodsnout
  tip West back to Rog'mar's east side.
  turnin 96107
  accept 96108                          -- Poison Tips

step The vipers and the tallstriders
  tip The Glade Vipers hide in the long grass south-east of town; the Roving Tallstriders graze beside them. Cavalry Scout Alturin, an Alliance elite (level 45), rides the road from Terral's Watch to Wheeler's Grange along the grass's south-west edge: keep clear of him.
  collect 271776 x4 quest 96108.1       -- Glade Viper Venom

step Neza Bloodsnout
  turnin 96108

step Turner's Logging Camp
  tip South-west across the river to the Alliance lumber camp. The lumberjacks carry the axes. Loot Wood Bundles from the Peasant Woodpiles around the camp and use them to fletch Makeshift Stickin' Spears. Ghostmaw, an elite (level 42), prowls the river by the camp: if he comes your way, back off and let him pass.
  collect 263972 x10 quest 93788.1      -- Woodworker's Axe
  collect 271629 @39.2,62.8             -- Wood Bundle, from the Peasant Woodpiles
  use 271629 quest 95951.1 @39.2,62.8   -- Wood Bundle: fletch it into Makeshift Stickin' Spears

step Meadowsbrook
  tip East to Meadowsbrook, the Alliance farm by the river: the farmhands work the fields and the feed satchels lie by the barns. Southern Watch, the Alliance outpost on the road, has guards: pass south of it.
  tip Careful: Ghostmaw, an elite (level 42), hunts along the river by the farm: keep an eye on the riverbank.
  kill 256383 x12 quest 93786.1         -- Meadowsbrook Farmhand
  collect 262640 x6 quest 93787.1       -- Feed Satchel

step Rog'mar
  tip Back to Rog'mar, where your Hearthstone is set: Tan'jani on the fort's west side first, then Krom'rosh, Gorg by the cook fire, Kreza and Neza on your way east through the fort.
  turnin 95951                          -- Tan'jani
  accept 95955                          -- Stick 'Em
  turnin 93786                          -- Krom'rosh
  turnin 93787
  accept 94483                          -- Show Them How It's Done
  turnin 93788                          -- Kreza Darkthorn

step The river and the Farholde camp
  tip South-west of Rog'mar the river runs between the farms: impale the Freshwater Crocolisks with Tan'jani's spears. The Alliance trains its scouts and priests at a camp on the far bank. Cavalry Scout Alturin, the Alliance elite, rides the road just east of the camp: pull the scouts and priests away from it.
  tip Careful: Ghostmaw, an elite (level 42), hunts along this river: if he comes your way, back off and let him pass.
  use 271639 quest 95955.1 @51.75,51.97 -- Tan'jani's spears, on the Freshwater Crocolisks in the river
  kill 270667 x8 quest 94483.1          -- Farholde Priest
  kill 257926 x12 quest 94483.2         -- Farholde Scout

step Rog'mar
  turnin 95955                          -- Tan'jani
  turnin 94483                          -- Krom'rosh

step Fuzzle
  tip Fuzzle wants out of Sunnyglade: lead him west to his treasure at the edge of town and keep the cultists off him.
  accept 94963                          -- Biting the Hand
  complete 94963 @41.6,47.7             -- lead Fuzzle out of Sunnyglade to his treasure, west of the town
  turnin 94963                          -- Fuzzle's Treasure

step WANTED: Scoutmaster Vargas
  when group 95882
  tip Scoutmaster Vargas is an elite (level 42) at the Alliance scouts' camp in the hills south-east of Na'zok, where you go next: grouping up is advised. The poster hangs in the middle of the fort; Neza Bloodsnout takes the eye, later in this guide.
  accept 95882                          -- the Wanted poster

step Scoutmaster Vargas
  when group 95882
  collect 268581 quest 95882.1 @75.4,34.3  -- Scoutmaster's Eye

step Powderfuse Port
  tip South-east down out of the hills to Powderfuse Port, the goblins' harbour on the coast. Friz Frazzlespark keeps a stall at the west end of the docks, Fimbo Greasemitz cooks by the inn, and Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz works the north pier.
  accept 95288                          -- Smuggler's Paradise
  accept 95121                          -- Fimbo Greasemitz: A Taste of the Sea
  accept 95254                          -- The WANTED! poster by the inn: Trapclaw
  accept 95118                          -- Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz: Saltwater Savages
  accept 95119                          -- Unfriendly Competition

step The murlocs, south-west
  tip South-west along the shore from the port: the saltwater murlocs camp on the beaches. On the way, a painted hide is stretched beside the path: it starts Terrors From the Deep for Argo Brinewhistle at the docks.
  collect 268344 x12 quest 95121.1      -- Saltwater Murloc Eye
  kill 256801 x8 quest 95118.1          -- Murloc Warrior
  kill 255898 x8 quest 95118.2          -- Murloc Oracle

step Back through the port
  tip Back north along the shore: hand in the murlocs and the hide on the docks on your way to the crawlers.
  turnin 95118                          -- Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz

step The crawlers and Trapclaw
  tip North along the beach from the docks: the crawlers drop the meat for Fimbo, and their entrails count for Argo. Trapclaw, a big crab, scuttles along the rocks east of the docks. Gul'gash, a rare elite of level 49, roams this coast from the docks up to the pirates' camp: if you see him, keep well away.
  collect 268345 x6 quest 95121.2       -- Sand Crawler Meat
  collect 268586 quest 95254.1          -- Trapclaw's Pincer

step The Eastsea pirates
  tip North-east along the coast to the pirates' camp on the cliffs. The buccaneers and musketeers carry the smuggled goods. Gul'gash walks the camp too: keep an eye out for him.
  kill 257901 x10 quest 95119.1         -- Eastsea Buccaneer
  kill 257910 x10 quest 95119.2         -- Eastsea Musketeer
  collect 268796 x8 quest 95288.1       -- Smuggled Goods

step Powderfuse Port
  tip Back to the port, from the north pier west through the docks.
  turnin 95119                          -- Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz
  accept 95122                          -- Unchecked Expansion
  accept 95123                          -- A Blast Ye Scurvy Dogs!
  turnin 95254                          -- Fimbo Greasemitz
  turnin 95121
  turnin 95288                          -- Friz Frazzlespark
  accept 95293                          -- Smuggler's Special: for Captain Bentcoin at the pirates' camp

step The pirates' second wave
  tip North along the coast from the port: the Eastsea raiders and bombardiers have dug in on the slopes west of the buccaneers' camp, among their powder kegs. Watch for Gul'gash on these cliffs.
  tip Careful: the Eastsea Raiders are level 44-45, a level or two over you here: pull them one at a time from the edge of the slopes and keep clear of the camp behind them.
  kill 257915 x8 quest 95122.1          -- Eastsea Raider
  kill 257916 x8 quest 95122.2 @79.1,33.8  -- Eastsea Bombardier
  collect 268346 x5 quest 95123.1       -- Eastsea Powder Keg

step Captain Bentcoin
  tip East along the cliffs to the far end of the pirates' camp: Captain Bentcoin waits by the water, Captain Haynes beside him.
  turnin 95293                          -- Captain Bentcoin

step Powderfuse Port
  tip Back to the port.
  turnin 95122                          -- Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz
  turnin 95123
  accept 95165                          -- See Ya, Scallywags!
  accept 95124                          -- Admiral Lamora
  accept 95296                          -- Friz: Shipping and Handling, for Wharfmaster Steamfizzle at Steamwheedle Port in the Feralas & Tanaris guide

step The pirates' ships
  tip Out to the pirates' cliffs once more. Plant Whizzbuzz's charges on the three ships moored below the camp, south to north; Admiral Lamora stands by the middle one, with her loot chest beside her. Keep an eye out for Gul'gash on the way.
  tip Careful: Admiral Lamora is level 45, a level or two over you here: clear the deck around her first and come in with full health.
  use 268505 quest 95165.3 @90.9,39.5   -- Remote Explosive Charge, the southern ship
  kill 257861 quest 95124.1             -- Admiral Lamora
  collect 268506 quest 95124.2          -- Lamora's Loot
  use 268505 quest 95165.2 @90.6,29.6   -- the middle ship
  use 268505 quest 95165.1 @88.3,25.8   -- the northern ship

step Powderfuse Port
  label argo
  tip Down to the port.
  turnin 95165                          -- Wharfmaster Whizzbuzz
  turnin 95124
  accept 95267 optional                 -- The Monster Surfaces: a big beast in the shallows south-west of the port, near Old Rot-Chum, the elite

step The Monster Surfaces
  when onquest 95267
  tip The Monstrous Threshadon prowls the shallows south-west of the port, below the murlocs' beaches. Old Rot-Chum, an elite, walks the shore close by: give him room.
  collect 268633 quest 95267.1          -- Sea Monster's Head

step Argo Brinewhistle
  when onquest 95267
  turnin 95267

# Riverglades for the Horde, part 4 of 4 (2026-11-12). Hand-written from players'
# recordings of the zone and Forever's quest data for titles, levels, objectives and places.
# Order: the hearth to Rog'mar; west through Sunnyglade to Da'grosh's camp below Twilight's
# Shroud, Crag'rog's cave, the Twilight cult's camps and ogre mine (levels 41-44); out through Twilight's Shroud to
# Kargath (its flight path), where the Feralas & Tanaris guide picks up.
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (players' recordings): The Wayward Warrior after Clugfist's Decree;
# Rise Up! and Death to the Executioner after Rumblings of Discontent; It Is Time, Brother... and Bring Me His Head
# after Carving a Path.
# Elites, behind a group choice: Overlord Kilgar (46). The Twilight camps hold elites the route
# never asks for: Twilight Enforcers (45) on patrol, Executioner Morg and Overlord Kilgar (46) in the fortress, the
# Twilight Forgemaster (46, rare).
# Left out on purpose:
# - Death to the Executioner (95433): Executioner Morg is an elite (46), and the mace goes to Clugfist in Bolder'ok.
# - A Token of Vengeance (94975), Tome of Twilight (94972), Eye of Mugg (94968) and Krol'dok Moulding (94973): their
#   items come from the Krol'dok Stronghold dungeon.
# - It Is Time, Brother... (95278): Da'grosh's message goes back to Krom'rosh in Rog'mar, and this route leaves the
#   zone through Twilight's Shroud instead.

step Rog'mar
  when onquest 95428
  tip Back to Rog'mar from the port, where your Hearthstone is set. Krom'rosh in the middle of the fort: Clugfist's word sends him looking for Da'grosh, his warrior in the west.
  turnin 95428                          -- Krom'rosh: Clugfist's Decree

step Neza Bloodsnout
  when onquest 95882
  turnin 95882

step Twilight's Shroud
  tip The next guide flies from Kargath in the Badlands: north out of Da'grosh's valley and up through Twilight's Shroud, the way through to the Badlands.
  goto 32.0,29.9 "Twilight's Shroud"

step Kargath
  tip Across the Badlands to Kargath, the Horde fortress built into the cliffs at the zone's western edge: its flight master stands at the foot of the fortress.
  enter "Badlands"
  zone Badlands
  getfp "Kargath"
